      ":question/id": "fae46a40-2aae-5529-b179-d96dd2b5205b",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(w+\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin w$ and $\\cos w$. Enter the signed coefficients.\n\n$\\cos\\left(w+\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin w\\,+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos w$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=w$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(w+\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\cos w\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\sin w\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos w\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\sin w\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin w-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos w.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
